## Steps to reproduce

1. `flutter create bug` and replace `lib/main.dart` with the sample below — a stock `MaterialApp` with **no** `SafeArea` and **no** `SystemChrome` calls, and `debugShowCheckedModeBanner` left at its default (`true`).
2. Run in **debug** mode on an Android device/emulator that has a status bar (reproduced here on a Samsung SM-S948B, Android 16 / API 36).
3. Look at the top-right corner where the `DEBUG` ribbon is painted.

## Expected results

The `DEBUG` `CheckedModeBanner` should remain fully visible, clear of the system status bar (as it did before edge-to-edge — the Android surface used to start *below* the status bar, so the banner sat just under it).

## Actual results

Under edge-to-edge (now the framework default on Android, flutter/flutter#182809, and OS-enforced on Android 15+), the app surface extends beneath the status bar. The `CheckedModeBanner` is painted at the raw top-right window corner and does **not** offset by `MediaQuery.viewPadding.top`, so the ribbon is drawn *behind* the status bar and is obscured by the system clock/battery/status icons.

In the attached screenshot the status-bar inset is `viewPadding.top = 37.33` (marked by the red strip), and the `DEBUG` ribbon renders inside that strip — the middle of the word `DEBUG` is hidden behind the battery indicator, leaving only `D…UG` legible.

Crucially, **there is no app-side remedy**: the banner is inserted by `MaterialApp`/`WidgetsApp` *above* the developer's tree, so it cannot be wrapped in `SafeArea`, and wrapping `MaterialApp` in `SafeArea` is neither correct nor effective. The only app-side lever is `debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false`, which removes the aid entirely. A framework fix would offset the debug banner by the top view padding so it stays within the safe area under edge-to-edge.

## Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(const DebugBannerRepro());

class DebugBannerRepro extends StatelessWidget {
  const DebugBannerRepro({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // `debugShowCheckedModeBanner` is true by default, so MaterialApp paints the
    // "DEBUG" CheckedModeBanner at BannerLocation.topEnd (top-right corner).
    //
    // Nothing here opts into edge-to-edge — it is now the framework default on
    // Android (flutter/flutter#182809). The Scaffold body therefore extends
    // under the status bar, and so does the debug banner, which is painted at
    // the raw window corner without offsetting by MediaQuery.viewPadding.top.
    return MaterialApp(
      home: Builder(
        builder: (context) {
          final topInset = MediaQuery.viewPaddingOf(context).top;
          return Scaffold(
            body: Stack(
              children: [
                // Visualise the status-bar strip the debug banner overlaps.
                Container(
                  height: topInset,
                  width: double.infinity,
                  color: Colors.red.withValues(alpha: 0.3),
                ),
                Center(
                  child: Text('Top viewPadding (status bar inset): $topInset px'),
                ),
              ],
            ),
          );
        },
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

</details>

## Screenshots or Video

<details open>
<summary>Screenshots / Video demonstration</summary>

<img width="480" height="260" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a36f0400-8a82-465a-90f0-84f2db67175b" />

</details>

