4. Observe bottom sheet opening animations and `ViewInsets` updating deltas

### Initial Investigation:
In 3.41,  `ViewInsets`'s updating deltas decrease to near zero.
In 3.44,  `ViewInsets`'s last updating delta is way largger.

If setting
```java
activity.getWindow().getDecorView().setSystemUiVisibility(View.SYSTEM_UI_FLAG_LAYOUT_STABLE
              | View.SYSTEM_UI_FLAG_LAYOUT_HIDE_NAVIGATION
              | View.SYSTEM_UI_FLAG_LAYOUT_FULLSCREEN);
```
 to enable `edgeToEdge` mode, which is the implementation in Flutter 3.41. It work as expected.

### Futher Investigation:
If modified the System NavigationBar height via `xposed`.
`ViewInsets`'s last updating delta roughly equals to the modified NavigationBar height.
So the last updating delta is very likely the NavigationBar height, which makes the bottom sheet animation jump at the end.

Reproduced on Android 11, 13, 14.

### Expected results

In 3.41,  Bottom sheet opening animations looks smooth, `ViewInsets`'s updating deltas decrease to near zero.

### Actual results

In 3.44, Bottom sheet opening animations is jumping at the end, `ViewInsets`'s last updating delta is way largger.

