issues.body:
### Steps to reproduce

1. Launch the sample project, e.g. flutter run -d chrome
2. Focus is on row 0, card 0
3. Press the Down arrow key, focus lands on row 1, card 0, as expected.
4. Press the Up arrow key, focus lands on row 0, card 1, unexpected result

The bug was introduced by this commit: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/commit/b46a6aa9a69284250cbafc9a6a5143f0bf22025a

### Expected results

Pressing Down moves focus from r0c0 to r1c0. Pressing Up again should reverse that move and return focus to r0c0.

### Actual results

