## Steps to reproduce

1. Run the sample below on **Android 14 (API 34)**.
2. Tap `edgeToEdge`, then tap the text field to open the keyboard.
3. Watch the logged `viewInsets.bottom`.

## Expected results

The last value reported during the animation equals the settled value.

## Actual results

The animation converges, and then `viewInsets.bottom` jumps in a single frame. Pixel 6
emulator, API 34, gesture navigation (`viewPadding.bottom` = 24.0):

```
insets=310.1 delta=2.3
insets=311.6 delta=1.5
insets=312.0 delta=0.4    <- converged
insets=336.4 delta=24.4   <- settled value, one frame later
```

The jump (24.4) matches `viewPadding.bottom` (24.0) modulo dp rounding. Anything laid out
from `viewInsets.bottom` stays 24dp low for the whole opening animation and then snaps.

## What I measured

Same app and device, varying only the system UI mode and the OS version:

| | animation converges to | settled value | jump |
|---|---|---|---|
| API 34, `edgeToEdge` | 312.0 | 336.4 | **+24.4** |
| API 34, `manual` + `overlays: [SystemUiOverlay.bottom]` | 312.4 | 312.4 | none |
| API 35 emulator, both modes | — | — | none |
| Android 17 (Pixel 8 Pro), both modes | — | — | none |

In `manual` mode on API 34, `viewPadding.bottom` is 0.0; in `edgeToEdge` it is 24.0.

Closing shows the mirror image: the first reported value after the settled one is
`336.4 → 312.4` (−24.0), then the ramp down.

## Code sample

<details>
<summary>main.dart</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter/scheduler.dart';
import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

void main() {
  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  double? last;
  SchedulerBinding.instance.addPersistentFrameCallback((_) {
    final view = WidgetsBinding.instance.platformDispatcher.views.first;
    final i = view.viewInsets.bottom / view.devicePixelRatio;
    if (last == null || (i - last!).abs() > 0.01) {
      // ignore: avoid_print
      print('insets=${i.toStringAsFixed(1)} '
          'delta=${last == null ? 0 : (i - last!).toStringAsFixed(1)}');
      last = i;
    }
  });
  runApp(const MaterialApp(home: Home(), debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false));
}

class Home extends StatelessWidget {
  const Home({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // The UI layer is lifted by viewInsets, so a mismatch between the animated
    // and the settled value is visible as a jump.
    return Scaffold(
      resizeToAvoidBottomInset: false,
      body: Padding(
        padding: EdgeInsets.only(bottom: MediaQuery.viewInsetsOf(context).bottom),
        child: Column(
          children: [
            const SizedBox(height: 60),
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: () =>
                  SystemChrome.setEnabledSystemUIMode(SystemUiMode.edgeToEdge),
              child: const Text('edgeToEdge'),
            ),
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: () => SystemChrome.setEnabledSystemUIMode(
                  SystemUiMode.manual, overlays: const [SystemUiOverlay.bottom]),
              child: const Text('manual(bottom only)'),
            ),
            const Spacer(),
            Container(height: 8, color: Colors.red),
            const TextField(decoration: InputDecoration(hintText: 'tap me')),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

</details>

## Version

```
Flutter 3.44.5 - channel stable
Framework - revision f94f4fc76b (2026-07-06)
Engine - hash d3a3293399556a85388faf8c6f0723a7a5597aa8 (revision 83675ed276)
Tools - Dart 3.12.2
```

## Related

#168768, #89914 — same user-visible symptom, both closed as fixed.

