Title: [video_player_android] Video judders on Pixel 10 with textureView, smooth with platformView

Description:
# Body

## Steps to reproduce

1. On a Pixel 10, play a local 1080p50 MP4 (mine is a ~12 minute GoPro clip) with `VideoPlayerController.file`, default `viewType`.
2. Watch it for a few seconds.
3. Recreate the same controller with `viewType: VideoViewType.platformView` and play the same file.

## Notes

`video_player_android`'s README says `VideoViewType.platformView` is not recommended on Android because of . My player lives in a fixed panel rather than a scrolling list, so I haven't hit that, but it does mean "use platformView" isn't a general answer for anyone hitting this.

Possibly relevant: I couldn't find any call to `Surface.setFrameRate()` in the plugin, so the content frame rate and the display refresh rate are never reconciled on the texture path. Here that's 50fps content on a 120Hz panel.

## Feature request buried in this

I could not detect this condition from Dart at all. `FrameTiming` only sees Flutter's own cadence, and `VideoPlayerValue.position` is ExoPlayer's media clock so it advances smoothly regardless. ExoPlayer is already counting exactly the right thing — `AnalyticsListener.onDroppedVideoFrames` and `onVideoFrameProcessingOffset` — but the plugin doesn't surface it and I don't have a reference to the `ExoPlayer` instance. Exposing those would have turned a week of guessing into one number, and would let apps detect and work around this themselves.

## Versions

```
Flutter 3.44.9, Dart 3.12.2
video_player 2.13.0
video_player_android 2.12.0
video_player_platform_interface 6.9.0
```

Affected: Pixel 10 (Tensor G5), Android <FILL IN — Settings > About phone > Android version and build number>
Not affected: Galaxy S23, iPhone (various)

Clip: 1080p50, ~12 min, <FILL IN codec — H.264 or HEVC; `ffprobe` or MediaInfo will say>

### Expected results

Playback is smooth, as it is on every other device I've tried.

### Actual results

With the default `VideoViewType.textureView` the picture judders continuously — not a stall or a stutter every few seconds, a constant unevenness. With `VideoViewType.platformView` on the same phone, same file, same build, it's completely smooth.

## Why I think this is the texture path and not my app, the file, or the device

I spent a while ruling things out before filing, because it looked like an app problem:

- The same file plays smoothly in Google Photos on the same Pixel 10, so the device decodes it fine in real time.
- The same file plays smoothly in my app on a Galaxy S23 and an iPhone, so it isn't the file or my code.
- My app draws overlay widgets on top of the video. They're painted in the same Flutter frames as the video and they move smoothly while the video judders.
- I instrumented `SchedulerBinding.addTimingsCallback` during the juddering playback. On the affected device, while it was visibly juddering:
  - display at 120Hz, so an 8.3ms budget
  - average build 1.3ms, average raster 3.6ms
  - 17 frames of 3955 over budget (0.43%)
  - ~602 frames per 5040ms window, i.e. ~99.5% of vsyncs produced a frame
  - no buffering events

So Flutter is building and rasterising frames on time and delivering nearly every vsync. What's uneven is which decoded image ends up in them.

For contrast, a second Android device that was *visibly smooth* delivered ~97% of vsyncs in the same measurement — worse on paper, better to look at. Frame production isn't what separates them.

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'dart:io';

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter/scheduler.dart';
import 'package:video_player/video_player.dart';

/// Any local 1080p50 clip reproduces it. Mine is a ~12 minute GoPro file.
const String videoPath = '/sdcard/Movies/GH022831.MP4';

void main() => runApp(const ReproApp());

class ReproApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const ReproApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => const MaterialApp(home: ReproPage());
}

class ReproPage extends StatefulWidget {
  const ReproPage({super.key});

  @override
  State<ReproPage> createState() => _ReproPageState();
}

class _ReproPageState extends State<ReproPage> {
  VideoPlayerController? _controller;
  VideoViewType _viewType = VideoViewType.textureView;

  // Frame timings, so you can see Flutter keeping up while the video judders.
  final Stopwatch _window = Stopwatch();
  int _frames = 0;
  int _late = 0;
  int _buildMicros = 0;
  int _rasterMicros = 0;
  String _summary = 'measuring...';

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    SchedulerBinding.instance.addTimingsCallback(_onTimings);
    _open();
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    SchedulerBinding.instance.removeTimingsCallback(_onTimings);
    _controller?.dispose();
    _window.stop();
    super.dispose();
  }

  double get _refreshHz =>
      SchedulerBinding
          .instance
          .platformDispatcher
          .implicitView
          ?.display
          .refreshRate ??
      60;

  void _onTimings(List<FrameTiming> timings) {
    final refreshHz = _refreshHz;
    final budgetMicros = (1000000 / refreshHz).round();
    for (final timing in timings) {
      _frames++;
      _buildMicros += timing.buildDuration.inMicroseconds;
      _rasterMicros += timing.rasterDuration.inMicroseconds;
      if (timing.buildDuration.inMicroseconds > budgetMicros ||
          timing.rasterDuration.inMicroseconds > budgetMicros) {
        _late++;
      }
    }
    if (_frames == 0 || _window.elapsed < const Duration(seconds: 5)) {
      return;
    }
    // Frames produced vs vsyncs that elapsed. A frame the engine never built
    // emits no FrameTiming at all, so it cannot show up as "over budget".
    final expected = (_window.elapsedMilliseconds * refreshHz / 1000).round();
    final summary =
        '${refreshHz.round()}Hz, budget ${(budgetMicros / 1000).toStringAsFixed(1)}ms\n'
        '$_frames frames of ~$expected vsyncs, $_late over budget\n'
        'avg build ${(_buildMicros / _frames / 1000).toStringAsFixed(1)}ms, '
        'avg raster ${(_rasterMicros / _frames / 1000).toStringAsFixed(1)}ms';
    _frames = 0;
    _late = 0;
    _buildMicros = 0;
    _rasterMicros = 0;
    _window
      ..reset()
      ..start();
    if (mounted) {
      setState(() => _summary = summary);
    }
  }

  Future<void> _open() async {
    final previous = _controller;
    setState(() => _controller = null);
    await previous?.dispose();

    final controller = VideoPlayerController.file(
      File(videoPath),
      viewType: _viewType,
    );
    await controller.initialize();
    await controller.setLooping(true);
    await controller.play();

    _frames = 0;
    _late = 0;
    _buildMicros = 0;
    _rasterMicros = 0;
    _window
      ..reset()
      ..start();

    if (!mounted) {
      await controller.dispose();
      return;
    }
    setState(() => _controller = controller);
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final controller = _controller;
    return Scaffold(
      backgroundColor: Colors.black,
      body: SafeArea(
        child: Column(
          children: [
            Expanded(
              child: Center(
                child: controller == null
                    ? const CircularProgressIndicator()
                    : AspectRatio(
                        aspectRatio: controller.value.aspectRatio,
                        child: VideoPlayer(controller),
                      ),
              ),
            ),
            SegmentedButton<VideoViewType>(
              segments: const [
                ButtonSegment(
                  value: VideoViewType.textureView,

                ),
                ButtonSegment(
                  value: VideoViewType.platformView,

                ),
              ],
              selected: {_viewType},
              onSelectionChanged: (selection) {
                setState(() => _viewType = selection.first);
                _open();
              },
            ),
            Padding(
              padding: const EdgeInsets.all(8),
              child: Text(
                _summary,
                textAlign: TextAlign.center,
                style: const TextStyle(color: Colors.white, fontSize: 12),
              ),
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

