issues.body:
### Steps to reproduce

A tooltip that is still on screen when an opaque route is pushed over its owner leaves its overlay child mounted but *offstage*. On the next window resize, two framework assertions fire.

Reached entirely through ordinary public API — `IconButton(tooltip: ...)` plus `Navigator.push` — with no custom `OverlayPortal` or render objects.

Self-contained, fully headless test (no window, no manual interaction). Save as `test/assertion_repro_test.dart` in a fresh `flutter create` project and run `flutter test`:

```dart
import 'package:flutter/gestures.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

/// Self-verifying repro: this test PASSES while the framework bug is present
/// and FAILS once it is fixed, so it can be used to bisect or to confirm a
/// patch. Fully headless — the resize is driven through `tester.view`.
///
/// Mechanism: a tooltip is on screen when an opaque route is pushed over its
/// owner. The tooltip's overlay child stays mounted, but its OverlayEntry is
/// now obstructed, so `_RenderTheater` skips laying it out (`skipCount`).
/// On the next resize the theater changes size while the skipped deferred
/// box keeps its pre-resize size, and `_RenderLayoutBuilder` — which is
/// `sizedByParent` with `size = constraints.biggest` — no longer matches.
void main() {
  testWidgets('offstage tooltip + resize trips two framework assertions', (
    tester,
  ) async {
    addTearDown(tester.view.reset);
    tester.view.devicePixelRatio = 1.0;
    tester.view.physicalSize = const Size(1200, 800);

    final errors = <String>[];
    final prior = FlutterError.onError;
    FlutterError.onError = (d) => errors.add(d.exceptionAsString());
    addTearDown(() => FlutterError.onError = prior);

    await tester.pumpWidget(
      MaterialApp(
        home: Builder(
          builder: (context) => Scaffold(
            body: Align(
              alignment: Alignment.topRight,
              child: IconButton(
                tooltip: 'Settings',
                icon: const Icon(Icons.settings),
                onPressed: () => Navigator.of(context).push(
                  PageRouteBuilder<void>(
                    pageBuilder: (_, _, _) =>
                        const Scaffold(body: Center(child: Text('settings'))),
                    transitionDuration: Duration.zero,
                    reverseTransitionDuration: Duration.zero,
                  ),
                ),
              ),
            ),
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );

    // 1. Hover the button so its tooltip opens.
    final mouse = await tester.createGesture(kind: PointerDeviceKind.mouse);
    await mouse.addPointer(location: Offset.zero);
    addTearDown(mouse.removePointer);
    await mouse.moveTo(tester.getCenter(find.byType(IconButton)));
    await tester.pump();
    await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 1));
    expect(find.text('Settings'), findsOneWidget, reason: 'tooltip is open');

    // 2. Click through to an opaque route while the tooltip is still up. Its
    //    owner is now under TickerMode(enabled: false), so the fade-out never
    //    ticks and the overlay child stays mounted but offstage.
    await tester.tap(find.byType(IconButton), warnIfMissed: false);
    await tester.pump();
