issues.body:
### Use case

In our banking app the user has to attach an account statement from another bank, so we open that bank's app by its deep link:

```
await launchUrl(Uri.parse('<bank-scheme>://'), mode: 
LaunchMode.externalApplication);
```

On Android the third-party app starts inside our task: Recents shows a single card, Back from the bank app drops the user into the middle of our flow, and re-opening our app from the launcher lands on the bank's screen. We want what tapping the bank's icon in the launcher does — its own task, two cards in Recents. That is also what already happens on iOS, so identical Dart code behaves differently per platform and the API gives us no way to say which we want.

Unlike #75584, this is not about the Back button (it works) but about task identity.

We ended up writing our own MethodChannel duplicating url_launcher just to add one Intent flag.


### Proposal

An opt-in way to add Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK with LaunchMode.externalApplication on Android. Either an Android-specific option on launchUrl, next to the existing webViewConfiguration / browserConfiguration, or a separate LaunchMode value; I'd follow whichever the team prefers.

@bruce3x already posted a working patch in #153901:

```
ActivityInfo activityInfo = launchIntent.resolveActivityInfo(activity.getPackageManager(), 0);
   boolean isOurApp =
       activityInfo != null && activity.getPackageName().equals(activityInfo.packageName);
   if (!isOurApp) {
    launchIntent.addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK);
   }
```

Prior issues: #153901 asked for the same flag and was closed by the no-response bot, thread now locked. #75584 was closed in 2023 with "use LaunchMode.externalApplication"; we do, and its closing comment itself notes the app "does still open in the same Flutter sandbox".

